Intercom local/cloud speech and wake-word qualification

Workstream ID: ic-05
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/Intercom/issues/4
Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: Evidence-backed speech selection and wake conversation contract
Dependencies: ic-01

Purpose:
  Compare local and cloud speech before selection and qualify local wake-only
  standby. The owner's later request selects installed local English speech
  and click-on/click-off capture for a bounded prototype; no cloud audio or wake
  standby is authorized by that exception.

Tasks:
  [x] Implement the selected installed-Windows English push-to-talk prototype.
  [x] Verify local recognition retains multiple phrases through stream completion.
  [ ] Select test hardware, languages, phrase, datasets and resource/latency budgets.
  [ ] Obtain audio/provider consent and choose one viable local/cloud candidate.
  [ ] Verify exact model/voice licenses, packaging and provider data/cost terms.
  [ ] Measure wake/recognition errors, response timing and concurrent resources.
  [ ] Qualify speed-first defaults and compare selectable processing priorities.
  [ ] Test echo, speech interruption, device loss and offline behavior.
  [ ] Qualify Windows endpoint AEC and label any half-duplex fallback honestly.
  [ ] Record human listening results and an explicit provider/privacy decision.

Acceptance criteria:
  Same-scenario comparison distinguishes facts, measurements and user preference.
  Wake standby stays local; the chosen phrase and timeout are documented.
  No silent cloud failover or raw-audio persistence by default.
  Voice activity detection is not represented as echo cancellation/authentication.
  Local speech is not misrepresented as fully offline Copilot execution.
  Results and selected contracts inform ic-02 before desktop implementation.
  Performance/speed is evaluated first; error rates and useful-response latency
  are reported together, not just time to a generic acknowledgment.
  Native binding support is not exact model/license/device qualification.

Completion evidence:
  Installed en-US System.Speech recognizer transcribes locally synthesized
  "Hello world. Please say hello world." as
  "Hello world please say hello world", confidence 0.9176309108734131.
  Multiple-phrase events avoid silently losing speech after a pause.
  Selected-device AudioWorklet capture, canonical PCM, level meter, cleanup,
  review-before-send and visible recognition failures pass Electron tests with
  deterministic synthetic audio. Silence/short input, low confidence and
  overlong input are rejected without dispatch. Browser DSP is disabled for
  this half-duplex path; playback stops before recording.
  Actual packaged synthetic-microphone capture transcribes "Say hello world";
  the existing Copilot session answers "Hello world." and native local playback
  completes without reported error. The single 67,370 ms run includes connection,
  recording and playback, not a component latency benchmark or qualified SLO.
  No physical FDUCE, multilingual quality, human listening, AEC, wake word,
  broad provider comparison or latency/resource budget is qualified.
  The .4 native source work test also captured synthetic "Say hello world",
  then required separate visible task review/confirmation before one approved
  read-only command. Actual response playback completed. Background completion
  speech is observed once, never replayed from restored receipts; deterministic
  packaged cases cover that UI behavior. No new physical/audio-quality claim.
  Candidate picks and reproducible evidence plan are in
  docs/technology-decisions.md and docs/performance-and-qualification.md.

Completion log:
  2026-11-11 - Extended voice destinations to reviewed background/terminal
    proposals without allowing a spoken proposal alone to dispatch work.
    Verified synthetic speech through one explicitly approved real background
    task and completed local speech; retained human/device/performance gates.
  2026-11-11 - Integrated packaged speech/Copilot round trip passed using locally
    synthesized input. This does not establish physical FDUCE acoustics or
    subjective listening quality. Kept raw audio in memory only.
  2026-11-11 - Owner selected click-on/click-off recording and installed local
    English recognition without model downloads. Implemented the bounded path;
    fixed native stream-end/phrase handling and verified synthetic recognition.
    Installed local speech is not fully offline Copilot execution.
  2026-11-10 - Planned after the user requested research of both speech approaches.
  2026-11-10 - Deepened native/cloud shortlist, audio/AEC and measurement gates;
    no capture, model download, cloud test or human listening performed.
